<Wiki
  title="New project"
  description="Create a PUV project, pin a PHP patch, add Packagist packages, and run a file."
>
  <p class="kicker">Wiki</p>
  <h1>New project</h1>
  <p>
    This is the path from an empty directory to a running file. Install is the
    <a href="/wiki/install">previous page</a>. Each command below has its own page when you want
    the variants.
  </p>
  <pre class="block">puv init
puv use 8.4
puv add symfony/console
puv add --dev phpunit/phpunit
puv run src/main.php
puv check
puv build</pre>

  <h2>What that sequence does</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <a href="/wiki/commands/init"><code>puv init</code></a> starts the project in the current
      directory. <code>puv init my-app</code> creates the directory first.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/wiki/commands/use"><code>puv use 8.4</code></a> installs the newest 8.4 patch and
      records that exact version. <code>puv use 8.4.23</code> stays on 8.4.23.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/wiki/commands/add"><code>puv add</code></a> records the dependency, resolves,
      writes <code>puv.lock</code>, and installs. <code>--dev</code> lands under
      <code>[dev-dependencies]</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/wiki/commands/run"><code>puv run src/main.php</code></a> runs that file on the
      project runtime. The generated autoloader is already prepended.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/wiki/commands/check"><code>puv check</code></a> reports syntax and project
      consistency, including when nothing is wrong.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/wiki/commands/build"><code>puv build</code></a> runs the <code>build</code> script,
      or writes <code>dist/</code> when the manifest has no such script.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>A skeleton instead of an empty project</h2>
  <pre class="block">puv create laravel blog
puv create codeigniter
puv create symfony
puv create slim</pre>
  <p>
    <a href="/wiki/commands/create"><code>puv create</code></a> fetches an application skeleton.
    With no template name, a terminal asks which one to use. A <code>composer.json</code> in the
    skeleton is imported with <a href="/wiki/commands/contain"><code>contain</code></a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    The manifest, the lock, and the directories they produce are
    <a href="/wiki/files">files</a>. A tree that already has Composer files is an
    <a href="/wiki/existing-project">existing project</a>.
  </p>
</Wiki>
